      Introduce a ``combining'' map that
      takes two polynomials $f, g \in \ideg_{d,m}(\F_q)$ and returns a new polynomial $\combine_{f,g} \in \ideg_{d,
        2m+2}(\F_q)$ defined by
      \[ \combine_{f,g}(\underbrace{x}_{\in \F_q^{m}},
